Bollywood superstar Shah Rukh Khan marked his 61st birthday with a special treat for fans, unveiling Tu Mil Jaaye, the first song from his much-awaited film King, as birthday wishes poured in from family, friends and colleagues across the film industry.
From his daughter Suhana Khan sharing a heartfelt tribute to Kajol, Kareena Kapoor Khan, Shilpa Shetty and Anil Kapoor celebrating the actor, the occasion highlighted the affection he continues to command across Bollywood.
The celebrations also extended to Mumbai, where fans gathered outside his residence, Mannat, to mark the birthday of the man fondly known as Bollywood's King Khan.
Screengrab: suhanakhan2, theshilpashetty/Instagram
Shah Rukh's daughter Suhana Khan took to Instagram to celebrate her father, sharing a picture of the poster of his upcoming film King. Keeping her message short and sweet, she wrote, &quot;Happy birthday king.&quot;
Shilpa Shetty also shared a loving birthday tribute on her Instagram Story, calling Shah Rukh her forever Baazigar. Sharing a picture with the superstar, she wrote, &quot;To the one and only King Khan. My forever Baazigar, who wins in every heartbeat. Happy birthday, wishing you endless love, laughter, great health and happiness always.&quot;
Screengrab: sonamkapoor, kajol/Instagram
Sonam Kapoor also wished the superstar with a warm message on her Instagram Story. &quot;Happy happy birthday Shah Rukh Khan. Lots and lots of love to you, always! Can't wait to see you in King,&quot; she wrote.
Kajol, who shares a much-loved on-screen history with Shah Rukh, also sent him birthday wishes. Sharing a message on her Instagram Story, she wrote, &quot;Happy Birthday SRK! Stay the absolute rockstar that you are. Sending you the biggest hug today!&quot;
