Kareena Kapoor Khan also joined the celebrations with a special Instagram post, sharing a glimpse connected to King. Her caption read, &quot;Happy Birthday King. The forever Ruler of the kingdom. Let's dance together... Can't wait. 24-12-26.&quot;
Her message also sparked excitement about what appears to be a special dance collaboration in the upcoming film.
Anil Kapoor, meanwhile, shared a nostalgic birthday message on X, reflecting on the years of friendship and memories he shares with Shah Rukh.
Happy Birthday, Shahrukh! ❤️ Years of laughter, countless memories and you haven&rsquo;t lost an ounce of that charm or madness and clearly neither of us is counting the years. Here&rsquo;s to many more. Jaldi milte hai, Lots of love always! 🤗 @iamsrk pic.twitter.com/AADGn9S4IU
&mdash; Anil Kapoor (@AnilKapoor) November 2, 2026
He wrote, &quot;Happy Birthday, Shah Rukh! ❤️ Years of laughter, countless memories and you haven't lost an ounce of that charm or madness and clearly neither of us is counting the years. Here's to many more. Jaldi milte hai, Lots of love always!&quot;
Filmmaker Karan Johar also joined the celebrations, sharing a picture of Shah Rukh looking dapper and noticeably fit for his upcoming film. Praising the actor's appearance, Karan wrote, &quot;61? Never looked this fine.&quot;
Screengrab: karanjohar/Instagram
Shah Rukh also shared a moment of his own with fans.
Taking to X, the actor posted a photograph of the Bandra-Worli Sea Link illuminated with his pictures and birthday wishes.
