&#8220;After two years of chaos and cruelty and corruption and incompetence, the likes of which we have not seen in the modern era, you get a chance to say, &#8216;Enough is enough,'&#8221; Obama declared in Cleveland.&nbsp;&#8220;We are voting for change right here in Ohio.&#8221;
The 65-year-old Democrat blamed the Trump administration for the rising cost of living, a top voter concern amid soaring fuel prices.
&#8220;The current president chose to make a series of bad decisions,&#8221; Obama said. &#8220;Most importantly, he decided to start an unnecessary war that nobody asked for.&#8221;
Obama also urged voters to cast their ballots as soon as possible since early voting is already open in this northern industrial state.
